This requirement applies even if the modified Software is never distributed as an installable application.
Examples include:
Hosting a modified PrivCord messaging service.
Operating a modified server or backend based on PrivCord.
Providing modified PrivCord functionality through a website.
Offering a modified version of PrivCord as an online service.
Operating a modified version that users access through an application or network connection.
Merely operating an unmodified version of the original Software does not, by itself, require publication of private configuration or deployment information.
